# Open Offer Builder - Project Context

## Overview
This is an open-source offer management system built on the Twenty CRM architecture. It focuses on creating, managing, and previewing offers stored in Twenty CRM's `agencyOffers` object.

## Key Technologies
- **Backend**: Node.js, Express, TypeScript, Twenty CRM REST API
- **Frontend**: React 18, Vite, TypeScript, Tailwind CSS, TanStack Query
- **Design System**: Twenty CRM style (use `--ods-*` CSS variables)

## Twenty CRM Integration
- Base URL: `https://twenty.inferencesaver.com/rest`
- Object: `agencyOffers`
- Fields: title, name, heroH1, heroLede (rich text), videoUrl
- Authentication: JWT tokens stored in localStorage as `offer-builder-token`

## API Endpoints
- `GET /api/offers` - List all offers
- `GET /api/offers/:id` - Get single offer
- `POST /api/offers` - Create offer
- `PATCH /api/offers/:id` - Update offer
- `DELETE /api/offers/:id` - Delete offer
- `GET /preview/:industryId/:id` - Public preview (no auth needed)

## Design Patterns
- Use `WidgetCard` for all card containers
- Use `Badge` for status indicators and relation displays
- Use `@floating-ui/react` with `FloatingPortal` for dropdowns
- Tables should be full-bleed (no outer padding)
- Keep heights on 4px grid (28px small, 40px medium)

## Component Index
- `Layout.tsx` - App shell with sidebar navigation
- `WidgetCard.tsx` - Twenty-style card component
- `Badge.tsx` - Status/styled badge component
- `Toast.tsx` - Notification system with provider
- `Spinner.tsx` - Loading indicator
- `OffersPage.tsx` - Table view of all offers
- `OfferDetailPage.tsx` - Form builder for editing offers
- `PreviewPage.tsx` - Public preview rendering

## Important Notes
- Never hardcode hex colors; use `--ods-*` CSS variables
- Use `useQuery` and `useMutation` from TanStack Query for data fetching
- All API calls go through `/api/*` proxy (Vite dev proxy configured)
- Preview route is public and doesn't require authentication
- The project reuses backend infrastructure from open-twenty-dialer but strips non-offer functionality
